# Record Created / Last Updated Timestamps

When creating or editing a `SKILL.md` or other markdown documentation
(guides, references, READMEs, PRDs, etc.), record when it was created and
when it was last changed.

This does **not** apply to `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` rule files -- rules stay
timestamp-free.

- Place a single metadata line near the top of the document, right after
  the title (or after a "Verified against" line if one exists):

  ```
  **Created:** YYYY-MM-DD · **Last updated:** YYYY-MM-DD
  ```

- Use today's date (from the current session/system date) in `YYYY-MM-DD`
  format.
- **New document**: set both `Created` and `Last updated` to today's date.
- **Editing an existing document**: keep `Created` unchanged, update
  `Last updated` to today's date.
- If a document already has a changelog/version-history section, you may
  record the date there instead of adding a separate metadata line, but
  don't do both.
- Skip this for generated/imported files (e.g. PDF-to-markdown conversions)
  that aren't hand-authored.
